---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="A server fails: how long do users keep hitting it?" hint="A customer's primary server dies. Choose the TTL, the health check, how resolvers treat the TTL, and whether response rate limiting is on, and see what users, the name servers and a spoofed flood experience.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default has a <b>one-hour TTL</b>: the health check marks the server dead in about 35 seconds, but resolvers keep handing out the dead address, so users are affected for <b>about half an hour on average</b> (an hour at worst). The cache, not the detection, is the slow part. The flood with <b>RRL off</b> becomes a <b>3.4 Gbps</b> stream to the victim, 20 times what the attacker sent.</li>
    <li>Set the TTL to <b>30 seconds</b>: users recover in <b>under a minute on average</b>, but the name servers answer <b>120 times more queries</b> and a quarter of lookups wait for a cache miss. Now set resolvers to <b>keep answers for an hour</b> and the short TTL buys nothing.</li>
    <li>Turn <b>RRL on</b>: the flood to the victim falls to about <b>0.1 Gbps</b>. With the 30-second TTL, though, a big resolver farm behind one network prefix sends <b>33 queries per second</b> for the name, and 85% of them are limited. Choose <b>big resolvers allowed</b> to keep the protection without the damage.</li>
    <li>Set the threshold to <b>1</b> and the interval to <b>10 s</b>: detection is fastest, but a single lost probe now triggers a <b>false failover about 86 times a day</b>.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg dnsb" data-dnsb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>TTL <select class="pg-in" data-ttl><option value="30">30 seconds</option><option value="300">5 minutes</option><option value="3600" selected>1 hour</option></select></label>
      <label>Health check every <select class="pg-in" data-iv><option value="10" selected>10 seconds</option><option value="30">30 seconds</option><option value="60">60 seconds</option></select></label>
      <label>Marked down after <select class="pg-in" data-th><option value="1">1 failure</option><option value="2">2 failures</option><option value="3" selected>3 failures</option><option value="5">5 failures</option></select></label>
      <label>Resolvers <select class="pg-in" data-mode><option value="respect" selected>respect the TTL</option><option value="min">raise it to at least 5 minutes</option><option value="hold">keep answers for 1 hour</option></select></label>
      <label>Response rate limiting <select class="pg-in" data-rrl><option value="off" selected>off</option><option value="on">on for everyone</option><option value="allow">on, big resolvers allowed</option></select></label>
      <label>Spoofed queries per second (thousands) <input type="range" min="50" max="1000" step="50" value="300" data-atk /> <b data-atkval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" data-bars>
      <h3>Share of resolvers still giving out the dead address</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Users on the dead server</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Name server load</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Cache misses</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>False failovers</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Flood reaching the victim</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b6><h3>Big resolver farm</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o6></span><span class="pg-note" data-n6></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 2,000 sample resolvers whose caches expire at random moments. The server fails at time 0 and the health check finds it after interval times threshold (the worst case), plus 5 seconds to publish; a resolver switches at its first cache expiry after that, and a resolver that refreshes in between gets the dead address again with a fresh TTL. The site gets 1,000 requests per second. Load assumes 200,000 resolver caches ask for this name whenever their copy expires. Each cache looks the name up once every 10 seconds, a miss costs 30 ms, and 1% of probes fail by chance, independently. The flood sends 70-byte queries, a signed answer is 1,400 bytes, a truncated reply is 90 bytes. RRL allows 5 full answers per second for each prefix and name, and every second excess one becomes a truncated reply. The big resolver farm is 1,000 caches sharing one /24, so it sends 1,000 divided by the TTL queries per second for this name.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style is:global>
  .playground .dnsb-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr) max-content; gap: 8px; align-items: center; font-size: .85rem; }
  .playground .dnsb-row .lbl { white-space: nowrap; color: var(--muted); }
  .playground .dnsb-row .pct { font: .82rem ui-monospace, monospace; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
  .playground .dnsb-track { height: 10px; border-radius: 5px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .dnsb-fill { height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--bad); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) { .playground .dnsb-fill { transition: width .25s; }}
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-dnsb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const N = 2000; const CACHES = 200000; const PROPAGATION = 5; const LOOKUP_RATE = 0.1; const MISS_MS = 30; const REQ_PER_S = 1000; const FARM = 1000; const LIMIT = 5;
    const MARKS: [string, number][] = [['10 s', 10], ['30 s', 30], ['1 min', 60], ['2 min', 120], ['5 min', 300], ['10 min', 600], ['20 min', 1200], ['40 min', 2400], ['1 hour', 3600], ['65 min', 3900]];
    let seed = 53; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const phase = Array.from({ length: N }, () => rnd()); // where each resolver is in its cache cycle when the server fails
    const dur = (s: number) => (s < 90 ? `${Math.round(s)} s` : s < 5400 ? `${Math.round(s / 60)} min` : `${(s / 3600).toFixed(1)} h`);
    const num = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    function model(ttl: number, iv: number, th: number, mode: string, rrl: string, atk: number) {
      const eff = mode === 'respect' ? ttl : mode === 'min' ? Math.max(ttl, 300) : Math.max(ttl, 3600);
      const ready = iv * th + PROPAGATION;
      const sw = phase.map((u) => { const p = u * eff; return ready + ((((p - ready) % eff) + eff) % eff); }); // when each resolver first sees the healthy answer
      const sorted = [...sw].sort((a, b) => a - b);
      const mean = sw.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / N; const p95 = sorted[Math.floor(N * 0.95)]; const max = sorted[N - 1];
      const share = MARKS.map(([, t]) => sw.filter((s) => s > t).length / N);
      const qps = CACHES / eff; const base = CACHES / 3600;
      const miss = 1 / (1 + LOOKUP_RATE * eff);
      const falsePerDay = (86400 / iv) * Math.pow(0.01, th);
      const attackerGbps = (atk * 70 * 8) / 1e9;
      const victimGbps = rrl === 'off' ? (atk * 1400 * 8) / 1e9 : ((LIMIT * 1400 + ((atk - LIMIT) / 2) * 90) * 8) / 1e9;
      const farmRate = FARM / eff;
      const limited = rrl === 'on' ? Math.max(0, 1 - LIMIT / farmRate) : 0;
      return { eff, ready, mean, p95, max, share, qps, base, miss, falsePerDay, attackerGbps, victimGbps, farmRate, limited, failed: mean * REQ_PER_S };
    }
    const bars = MARKS.map(([label]) => {
      const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'dnsb-row';
      const l = document.createElement('span'); l.className = 'lbl'; l.textContent = `after ${label}`;
      const track = document.createElement('div'); track.className = 'dnsb-track'; const fill = document.createElement('div'); fill.className = 'dnsb-fill'; track.append(fill);
      const p = document.createElement('span'); p.className = 'pct';
      row.append(l, track, p); q('[data-bars]').append(row); return { fill, p };
    });
    function draw() {
      const ttl = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-ttl]').value); const iv = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-iv]').value); const th = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-th]').value);
      const mode = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mode]').value; const rrl = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-rrl]').value; const atk = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-atk]').value) * 1000;
      q('[data-atkval]').textContent = num(atk / 1000);
      const m = model(ttl, iv, th, mode, rrl, atk);
      bars.forEach((b, i) => { const pc = m.share[i] * 100; b.fill.style.width = `${pc}%`; b.p.textContent = `${pc.toFixed(pc > 0 && pc < 10 ? 1 : 0)}%`; });
      const set = (k: number, out: string, note: string, bad: boolean) => { q(`[data-o${k}]`).textContent = out; q(`[data-n${k}]`).textContent = note; q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${k}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'); };
      set(1, `${dur(m.mean)} on average`, `worst ${dur(m.max)}, 95th percentile ${dur(m.p95)}; ${num(m.failed)} failed requests. Detection and publishing take ${dur(m.ready)}; resolvers hold the old answer for up to ${dur(m.eff)}.`, m.mean > 90);
      set(2, `${num(m.qps)} queries/s`, m.qps > m.base * 1.5 ? `${num(m.qps / m.base)} times the load of a 1-hour TTL (${num(m.base)} per second)` : 'the minimum: resolvers keep answers for an hour', m.qps > 3000);
      set(3, `${(m.miss * 100).toFixed(m.miss < 0.01 ? 2 : 1)}% of lookups miss`, `+${(m.miss * MISS_MS).toFixed(1)} ms on average; ${m.miss > 0.01 ? `the slowest 1% of lookups wait ${MISS_MS} ms for the name server` : 'the 99th percentile is a cache hit'}`, m.miss > 0.1);
      set(4, m.falsePerDay >= 1 ? `${num(m.falsePerDay)} per day` : m.falsePerDay >= 0.1 ? `${m.falsePerDay.toFixed(1)} per day` : `1 in ${num(1 / m.falsePerDay)} days`, `a healthy server is marked down after ${th === 1 ? 'one lost probe' : `${th} lost probes in a row`}`, m.falsePerDay >= 0.1);
      set(5, `${m.victimGbps.toFixed(m.victimGbps < 1 ? 2 : 1)} Gbps`, `${(m.victimGbps / m.attackerGbps).toFixed(2)} times the ${m.attackerGbps.toFixed(2)} Gbps the attacker sent`, m.victimGbps > m.attackerGbps * 2);
      set(6, rrl === 'on' ? `${Math.round(m.limited * 100)}% of queries limited` : rrl === 'allow' ? 'not limited' : 'not limited (RRL off)', `${m.farmRate.toFixed(m.farmRate < 10 ? 2 : 1)} queries per second for one name from one prefix, against a limit of ${LIMIT}`, m.limited > 0.05);
      const cause = m.ready > m.eff ? `the health check needs ${dur(m.ready)} to find the failure and publish it, which is longer than the ${dur(m.eff)} cache` : `the health check took only ${dur(m.ready)}, and the rest is resolver caches holding the old address${mode === 'respect' ? '' : mode === 'min' ? ' because they raise short TTLs to 5 minutes' : ' because they ignore short TTLs'}`;
      const fo = m.mean > 90 ? `Users keep hitting the dead server for ${dur(m.mean)} on average and ${dur(m.max)} at worst: ${cause}.`
        : `Users recover in ${dur(m.mean)} on average and ${dur(m.max)} at worst. The price is ${num(m.qps)} queries per second at the name servers (${num(m.qps / m.base)} times a 1-hour TTL) and ${(m.miss * 100).toFixed(0)}% of lookups waiting for a cache miss.`;
      const at = rrl === 'off' ? `The spoofed flood of ${num(atk / 1000)}k queries per second turns into ${m.victimGbps.toFixed(1)} Gbps aimed at the victim, ${(m.victimGbps / m.attackerGbps).toFixed(0)} times what the attacker sent.`
        : `With RRL the victim gets ${m.victimGbps.toFixed(2)} Gbps instead of ${((atk * 1400 * 8) / 1e9).toFixed(1)}.${rrl === 'on' && m.limited > 0.05 ? ` But the big resolver farm loses ${Math.round(m.limited * 100)}% of its answers, because a short TTL makes it ask more often than the limit allows.` : rrl === 'allow' ? ' The big resolvers are exempt, so real traffic is not touched.' : ''}`;
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', m.mean > 90 || rrl === 'off' || m.limited > 0.05); out.textContent = `${fo} ${at}`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
